  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"211\" data-end=\"404\">The <strong data-start=\"215\" data-end=\"235\">aldosterone test</strong> measures the level of <strong data-start=\"258\" data-end=\"273\">aldosterone</strong>, a hormone produced by the <strong data-start=\"301\" data-end=\"319\">adrenal glands</strong>, which plays a vital role in <strong data-start=\"349\" data-end=\"401\">regulating sodium, potassium, and blood pressure</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"406\" data-end=\"439\">This test is primarily used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"440\" data-end=\"843\">\n<li data-start=\"440\" data-end=\"529\">\n<p data-start=\"442\" data-end=\"529\">Investigate <strong data-start=\"454\" data-end=\"480\">causes of hypertension</strong>, especially <strong data-start=\"493\" data-end=\"527\">resistant or early-onset cases</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"530\" data-end=\"667\">\n<p data-start=\"532\" data-end=\"667\">Diagnose <strong data-start=\"541\" data-end=\"584\">primary aldosteronism (Conn's syndrome)</strong> &ndash; a condition where excess aldosterone causes <strong data-start=\"631\" data-end=\"665\">hypertension and low potassium</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"668\" data-end=\"752\">\n<p data-start=\"670\" data-end=\"752\">Differentiate between <strong data-start=\"692\" data-end=\"703\">primary</strong> and <strong data-start=\"708\" data-end=\"728\">secondary causes</strong> of aldosterone excess</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"753\" data-end=\"843\">\n<p data-start=\"755\" data-end=\"843\">Evaluate <strong data-start=\"764\" data-end=\"784\">adrenal function</strong> in patients with suspected adrenal tumors or hyperplasia</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"845\" data-end=\"998\">Aldosterone is usually measured along with <strong data-start=\"888\" data-end=\"913\">plasma renin activity</strong> to calculate the <strong data-start=\"931\" data-end=\"964\">aldosterone-renin ratio (ARR)</strong>, which is critical for diagnosis.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1046\" data-end=\"1085\">High aldosterone levels may indicate:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1086\" data-end=\"1595\">\n<li data-start=\"1086\" data-end=\"1215\">\n<p data-start=\"1088\" data-end=\"1215\"><strong data-start=\"1088\" data-end=\"1136\">Primary hyperaldosteronism (Conn&rsquo;s syndrome)</strong> &ndash; autonomous secretion of aldosterone from an adrenal adenoma or hyperplasia</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1216\" data-end=\"1455\">\n<p data-start=\"1218\" data-end=\"1299\"><strong data-start=\"1218\" data-end=\"1250\">Secondary hyperaldosteronism</strong>, due to increased renin stimulation, often from:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1302\" data-end=\"1455\">\n<li data-start=\"1302\" data-end=\"1329\">\n<p data-start=\"1304\" data-end=\"1329\"><strong data-start=\"1304\" data-end=\"1329\">Renal artery stenosis</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1332\" data-end=\"1362\">\n<p data-start=\"1334\" data-end=\"1362\"><strong data-start=\"1334\" data-end=\"1362\">Congestive heart failure</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1365\" data-end=\"1393\">\n<p data-start=\"1367\" data-end=\"1393\"><strong data-start=\"1367\" data-end=\"1393\">Cirrhosis with ascites</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1396\" data-end=\"1420\">\n<p data-start=\"1398\" data-end=\"1420\"><strong data-start=\"1398\" data-end=\"1420\">Nephrotic syndrome</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1423\" data-end=\"1455\">\n<p data-start=\"1425\" data-end=\"1455\"><strong data-start=\"1425\" data-end=\"1455\">Dehydration or hypovolemia</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1456\" data-end=\"1500\">\n<p data-start=\"1458\" data-end=\"1500\"><strong data-start=\"1458\" data-end=\"1479\">Adrenal carcinoma</strong> (rare but serious)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1501\" data-end=\"1595\">\n<p data-start=\"1503\" data-end=\"1595\"><strong data-start=\"1503\" data-end=\"1533\">Excessive potassium intake</strong> or <strong data-start=\"1537\" data-end=\"1558\">low sodium intake</strong>, which stimulate aldosterone release</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1597\" data-end=\"1731\">In <strong data-start=\"1600\" data-end=\"1625\">primary aldosteronism</strong>, aldosterone is high while renin is low. In <strong data-start=\"1670\" data-end=\"1689\">secondary forms</strong>, both aldosterone and renin are elevated.</p>",
